><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Uemura</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kozaki</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakaguchi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The relationship  between cytotoxic effect and binding to mammalian cultured cells of  <italic>Clostridium perfringens</italic>enterotoxin</article-title><source>FEMS Microbiol Lett</source><year>1985</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>135</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Horiguchi</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Uemura</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamata</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kozaki</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakaguchi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Production and characterization of monoclonal antibodies to <italic>Clostridium perfringens</italic>enterotoxin</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>1986</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>31</fpage><lpage>35</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2870028</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Horiguchi</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Akai</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakaguchi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Isolation and function of a  <italic>Clostridium perfringens</italic>enterotoxin fragment</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>1987</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>2912</fpage><lpage>2915</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2890582</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ikeda</surname><give